{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1891","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Suspicious logarithms"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$f$$$($$$x$$$) be the floor of the binary logarithm of $$$x$$$. In other words, $$$f$$$($$$x$$$) is largest non-negative integer $$$y$$$, such that $$$2^y$$$ does not exceed $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$g$$$($$$x$$$) be the floor of the logarithm of $$$x$$$ with base $$$f$$$($$$x$$$). In other words, $$$g$$$($$$x$$$) is the largest non-negative integer $$$z$$$, such that $$${f(x)}^{z}$$$ does not exceed $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$q$$$ queries. The $$$i$$$-th query consists of two integers $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$. The answer to the query is the sum of $$$g$$$($$$k$$$) across all integers $$$k$$$, such that $$$l_i \\leq k \\leq r_i$$$. Since the answers might be large, print them modulo $$${10^9 + 7}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$q$$$ — the number of queries ($$$1 \\leq q \\leq 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$q$$$ lines each contain two integers $$$l_i$$$ and $$$r_i$$$ — the bounds of the $$$i$$$-th query ($$$4 \\leq l_i \\leq r_i \\leq 10^{18}$$